\begin_layout Standard
Question:
 Two boats,
 A and B,
 move away from a buoy anchored at the middle of a river along the mutually perpendicular straight lines:
 the boat A along the river,
 and the boat B across thg river.
 Having moved off an equal distance from the buoy the boats returned.
 Find the ratio of times of motion of boats 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau_{A}/\tau_{B}$
\end_inset

 if the velocity of each boat with respect to water is 
\begin_inset Formula $\eta$
\end_inset

 = 1.2 times greater than the stream velocity.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Solution:
 ->
